# Milestone: M3
# Covers: tag.stop() called with no active enclosing scope for that tag
#         propagates to fatal (unhandled TAG_STOP).
#
# blocked: tag.stop() outside an active scope returns nil instead of fatal; expected semantics not implemented — v1.0-rc
# matrix-row: tag-stop
#
# Reason: requires UTag runtime (T29) to distinguish "stop with no active
# scope" from a normal stop.  At M3, UEXEC_TAG_STOP with no matching
# TAG_SCOPE entry in the cleanup stack already escalates to fatal — but
# the tag type infrastructure to write a meaningful urbiscript test does not
# exist yet.  The behaviour is covered at the C level by
# test_capi_unwind.c::capi_tag_stop_local_deposits_tag_stop.
#
# When T29 lands, implement this fixture by uncommenting the source below.
# Expected behaviour: stopping a tag from outside its scope is a runtime error.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T29):
#   var t = Tag.new;
#   t.stop();
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] error: ...
